{"nodes":[{"id":"readme_elajgar","label":"Elajgar app","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A Next.js app for pain assessment, corrective exercise and nutrition tracking."},{"id":"readme_local_database","label":"Local MySQL development database","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Runs MySQL 8 via docker-compose.yml on port 3307 (avoids Windows MySQL on 3306), utf8mb4_unicode_ci for Persian text and case-insensitive contains searches, named volume so data survives docker compose down, health check so migrations never run against a still-starting server."},{"id":"readme_vazirmatn_font","label":"Vazirmatn self-hosted font","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Self-hosted from @fontsource/vazirmatn (lib/fonts.ts) because Google Fonts is blocked on many networks and next build treats a failed font fetch as a build error while next dev only warns; also avoids every visitor fetching the font from Google."},{"id":"readme_authentication","label":"Sign-in methods (SMS code and scrypt password)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"SMS code is the only way to create an account and always works as a fallback; password is optional, stored as a scrypt hash in its own table so it cannot leak into user queries; password sign-in is rate limited and unknown number/wrong password give the same answer to prevent phone-number enumeration."},{"id":"readme_pwa","label":"Progressive web app with service worker","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"manifest.json, icon.svg, sw.js and offline.html; nothing belonging to a user is cached so every /api/ request goes to the network; only content-hashed static files and icons are cached so the app shell opens offline; worker only registered in production builds."},{"id":"readme_db_doctor","label":"npm run db:doctor verification command","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"One command that verifies env vars, database connection, schema match against prisma/schema.prisma, admin panel access, Prisma client freshness, and SMS provider reachability/credit; the fastest way to find what is broken after a deploy or host migration."},{"id":"readme_admin_panel","label":"Admin panel at /panel-7x9k4m","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Deliberately unguessable path (not /admin) so scanners do not discover it; the role check is what actually protects it, the path is only the first line of defence; ADMIN role provisioned out of band via seed or admin:promote since there is no way to become admin through the app."},{"id":"readme_before_go_live","label":"Before-you-go-live checklist","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Development accounts and the development admin path are not for production; delete test accounts, change the admin path, check ADMIN_PHONE and sms.ir balance, move off the development database, rotate JWT_SECRET."},{"id":"readme_tests","label":"Tests and lint (npm test, npm run lint)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"readme_deploying","label":"Deploying section","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"deploy_liara_deployment","label":"Putting elajgar.ir online with Liara","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"deploy_liara_mysql","label":"MySQL database on Liara","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"App and database in the same Liara private network so the address points inside Liara's network; faster and traffic never goes to the internet."},{"id":"deploy_env_vars","label":"Liara server environment variables","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET, ADMIN_PHONE, SMSIR_API_KEY, SMSIR_TEMPLATE_ID, SMSIR_CODE_PARAM are set on the server, not in the project folder; full list with explanations in .env.production.example."},{"id":"deploy_liara_pre_start_sh","label":"liara_pre_start.sh startup script","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Runs on Liara's server before the app starts: builds the Prisma client there (the local build is for Windows and would not load), creates tables with prisma db push, and seeds foods/articles/exercises/plans/settings plus the ADMIN_PHONE admin role; safe to re-run on every restart."},{"id":"deploy_domain_dns_ssl","label":"Domain elajgar.ir, DNS records and SSL certificate","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Three DNS records (ALIAS/CNAME, TXT for ownership, CNAME for DNS-01 SSL) managed via IRNIC or synced if Liara's own DNS is used; SSL is free and self-renewing."},{"id":"deploy_updating","label":"Updating the app","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"deploy_troubleshooting","label":"Troubleshooting table","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"deploy_before_real_launch","label":"Before-real-launch checklist","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/DEPLOY.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"References the full list in the README under 'Before you go live': delete test users, change admin path, top up sms.ir balance, put a real JWT_SECRET in the console."},{"id":"howto_cpanel_deployment","label":"Upload and run Elajgar on a cPanel webhost","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"howto_build_locally","label":"Build locally (npm install, prisma generate, build)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Recommended because shared hosts often have limited memory and CPU; the build does not need Google Fonts since Vazirmatn is self-hosted from @fontsource/vazirmatn."},{"id":"howto_files_to_upload","label":"Files to upload (.next, prisma, public, package.json, package-lock.json, server.js, next.config.ts, .env)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"howto_env_vars","label":"cPanel environment variables","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"NODE_ENV=production, PORT=3000, DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET; DATABASE_URL keeps connection_limit (shared free tiers may allow only 20 concurrent connections vs Prisma's default pool of CPU cores x 2 + 1) and connect_timeout (Prisma default 5s is not enough for a managed service just powered on); sslmode=REQUIRED for hosted TLS."},{"id":"howto_database_setup","label":"Database setup (db:generate, db:push, db:doctor)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"scripts/prisma.mjs loads .env.local then .env so the same commands work locally and on the host, unlike plain npx prisma which only reads .env; db:push applies only the difference and never drops data; db:doctor verifies the whole stack."},{"id":"howto_seed_admin","label":"Seed food database and create admin account","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Seed writes Food rows plus partner gyms, editorial content and default health-score settings; ADMIN_PHONE (or ADMIN_PHONES) in .env gives the admin role on every run since there is no way to get ADMIN through the app; the user must have signed in at least once before admin:promote works."},{"id":"howto_start_app","label":"Start application (npm start / server.js)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"howto_updating_troubleshooting","label":"Updating later and troubleshooting","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/howto.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"cpanel_deployment_guide","label":"Step-by-step cPanel deployment","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"cpanel_database_provider","label":"Prisma schema MySQL provider","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"prisma/schema.prisma declares provider = \"mysql\"; mixing a PostgreSQL URL with the MySQL provider makes Prisma fail at startup, so provider and connection string must change together for PostgreSQL hosts."},{"id":"cpanel_server_js","label":"server.js for Phusion Passenger","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Phusion Passenger looks for a file named server.js to start the Node.js app; it wraps next() with createServer and getRequestHandler on PORT (default 3000)."},{"id":"cpanel_build_project","label":"Build project locally","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"cpanel_zip_files","label":"Zip files for upload","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Do not zip node_modules (too large, generated on cPanel); include .next, prisma, public, package.json, package-lock.json, server.js, next.config.ts."},{"id":"cpanel_create_database","label":"Create MySQL database in cPanel","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"cpanel_setup_nodejs_app","label":"Setup Node.js App in cPanel","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Node.js version 18+, Production mode, application root, startup file server.js; env vars NODE_ENV, JWT_SECRET, DATABASE_URL (mysql://USERNAME:PASSWORD@localhost:3306/DATABASENAME), SMSIR_API_KEY, SMSIR_TEMPLATE_ID, SMSIR_CODE_PARAM, optional NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN."},{"id":"cpanel_upload_files","label":"Upload files in cPanel","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"cpanel_run_final_commands","label":"Run final commands in cPanel terminal","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"npm install --production, npx prisma db push (applies only the difference, never drops data), npx prisma generate; after activating the Node.js environment."},{"id":"cpanel_restart_test","label":"Restart and test","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CPANEL_DEPLOYMENT.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},{"id":"claude_think_before_coding","label":"Think before coding guideline","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CLAUDE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"State assumptions explicitly, present multiple interpretations instead of picking silently, push back on overcomplication, stop and name what is confusing."},{"id":"claude_simplicity_first","label":"Simplicity first guideline","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CLAUDE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Minimum code that solves the problem, nothing speculative; no features beyond what was asked, no abstractions for single-use code, no error handling for impossible scenarios."},{"id":"claude_surgical_changes","label":"Surgical changes guideline","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CLAUDE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Touch only what you must; match existing style; remove only imports/variables/functions your own changes made unused; never remove pre-existing dead code unless asked."},{"id":"claude_goal_driven_execution","label":"Goal-driven execution guideline","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/CLAUDE.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Transform tasks into verifiable goals with success criteria and loop until verified; weak criteria require constant clarification."},{"id":"docker_compose_local_mysql","label":"Local MySQL for development","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/docker-compose.yml","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A local MySQL 8 database for development so the app does not depend on an external host; matching connection string in .env.exsample (mysql://elajgar:elajgar@127.0.0.1:3307/elajgar)."},{"id":"docker_compose_db_service","label":"db service (mysql:8.0)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/docker-compose.yml","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Container named elajgar-db, restarts unless stopped, character-set-server=utf8mb4 and collation-server=utf8mb4_unicode_ci for Persian text and case-insensitive contains searches."},{"id":"docker_compose_utf8mb4","label":"utf8mb4 character set and collation","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/docker-compose.yml","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"MySQL 8 defaults to a case-sensitive collation; the app's searches rely on contains matching 'MP4' against 'mp4' the way they do on the hosted database."},{"id":"docker_compose_named_volume","label":"db-data named volume","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/docker-compose.yml","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Named volume so the data survives docker compose down."},{"id":"docker_compose_healthcheck","label":"mysqladmin ping healthcheck","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/docker-compose.yml","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Compose reports the container healthy only when it accepts connections, so db push and the seed never run against a server still starting up; 5s interval, 5s timeout, 20 retries, 30s start period."}],"edges":[{"source":"readme_elajgar","target":"readme_local_database","relation":"references","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1.0,"source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"weight":1.0},{"source":"readme_elajgar","target":"readme_vazirmatn_font","relation":"references","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1.0,"source_file":"/Users/sadegh/Elajgar/README.md","source_location":null,"weight":1.0},{"source":"readme_elajgar","target":"readme_authentication","relation":"references","confidence":"EXT